---
title: Dragon Noodles
description: Spicy lo mein noodles tossed with egg scrambled in chile butter and a sriracha-soy sauce.
tags: [noodles]
course: main
difficulty: easy
source:
  name: Budget Bytes
  url: https://www.budgetbytes.com/spicy-noodles/
servings: 2
prep time: 5m
cook time: 10m
---

Begin to boil water for the noodles in a #pot{}. Once the water reaches a full boil, add the @lo mein noodles{113%g}(4 oz) and cook according to the package directions (boil for ~boil{5-7%minutes}).

While waiting for the water to boil, prepare the sauce. In a #small bowl{} stir together the @brown sugar{1%tbsp}, @soy sauce{1%tbsp}, and @sriracha{1%tbsp}(rooster sauce).

In a large #skillet{} melt the @butter{2%tbsp} over medium-low heat. Add the @red pepper flakes{1/4%tsp} to the butter as it melts.

Whisk the @egg{1}(large) in a #bowl{} and then add to the melted butter. Stir gently and cook through. Once the egg is done cooking, turn off the heat.

When the noodles are tender, drain the water and then add them to the skillet with the cooked egg. Also add the prepared sauce. Turn the heat on to low to evaporate excess moisture, and stir until everything is coated well with the sauce.

Sprinkle the @scallion{1}(sliced) and @fresh cilantro{1%handful}(leaves, whole) on top and serve.
